--indent 4
--ifdef no-indent
--allman false
--commas always
--semicolons never
--trimwhitespace always
--modifierorder nonisolated,open,public,internal,fileprivate,private,private(set),fileprivate(set),internal(set),public(set),open(set),override,final,required,convenience,weak,unowned,lazy,dynamic,mutating,nonmutating,class,static
--wraparguments before-first
--wrapcollections before-first
--swiftversion 6
--header ignore

# Disabled: these contradict the project's own style rules, which are the
# authoritative style gate.
# - enumNamespaces: rewrites static-only `struct` namespaces (e.g. `struct Key`) into `enum`,
#   but the namespace rule requires `struct` for caseless namespaces. Leaving it on
#   would have SwiftFormat and the style rules fight each other.
# - wrapSingleLineComments: would reflow doc comments, but the doc-comment rule owns
#   doc-comment formatting (one paragraph per line). Pre-emptive — inert today since no
#   --maxwidth is set, but disabled so it can never silently start wrapping them.
# - repeatedGuard (new in 0.64): folds consecutive guards that share an else body into one
#   condition list, hundreds of characters long where a function checks several things in
#   turn. The separate guards stay.
--disable enumNamespaces,wrapSingleLineComments,repeatedGuard

# These rules were checked against 0.64.0: an older formatter refuses rather than
# disagreeing. Raise it when a newer release has been checked the same way.
--minversion 0.64.0
